1
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:09,295
There's a kind of quiet that isn't peace.

2
00:00:09,295 --> 00:00:12,993
It's the quiet of a body that has decided, all by

3
00:00:12,993 --> 00:00:15,029
itself, to stop moving.

4
00:00:15,229 --> 00:00:18,467
I learned about that quiet on a massage table.

5
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,665
I'm a mother.

6
00:00:19,665 --> 00:00:23,505
I work with my hands, and I carry everything in my

7
00:00:23,505 --> 00:00:23,889
back.

8
00:00:23,889 --> 00:00:27,499
The kids, the bills, the school calls, the job.

9
00:00:27,499 --> 00:00:31,492
By the end of that winter I couldn't turn my head to

10
00:00:31,492 --> 00:00:33,328
check my blind spot.

11
00:00:33,528 --> 00:00:37,036
So I did the thing everybody says you should do.

12
00:00:37,036 --> 00:00:38,643
I took care of myself.

13
00:00:38,643 --> 00:00:40,332
I booked a massage.

14
00:00:40,532 --> 00:00:42,283
I'd been to him before.

15
00:00:42,283 --> 00:00:43,501
He was licensed.

16
00:00:43,501 --> 00:00:46,013
His certificate hung by the door.

17
00:00:46,013 --> 00:00:50,049
He knew my name, asked about my children, played soft

18
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:50,506
music.

19
00:00:50,506 --> 00:00:53,547
Nothing about that room said danger.

20
00:00:53,747 --> 00:00:56,746
That's the part people don't understand.

21
00:00:56,746 --> 00:00:59,371
It doesn't always look like danger.

22
00:00:59,371 --> 00:01:03,121
Sometimes it looks like a warm towel and a man who

23
00:01:03,121 --> 00:01:05,446
remembers your kids' names.

24
00:01:05,646 --> 00:01:08,351
He told me what every therapist says.

25
00:01:08,351 --> 00:01:09,594
"Get comfortable.

26
00:01:09,594 --> 00:01:10,763
Under the sheet.

27
00:01:10,763 --> 00:01:11,940
I'll knock."

28
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:13,341
I lay face down.

29
00:01:13,341 --> 00:01:14,467
I breathed out.

30
00:01:14,467 --> 00:01:18,368
For the first time in months, I let my guard all the

31
00:01:18,368 --> 00:01:19,344
way down.

32
00:01:21,044 --> 00:01:23,758
It started the way a massage starts.

33
00:01:23,758 --> 00:01:24,511
Shoulders.

34
00:01:24,511 --> 00:01:24,888
Back.

35
00:01:24,888 --> 00:01:27,827
Pressure that hurt in the good way.

36
00:01:28,027 --> 00:01:31,800
Then his hands went somewhere a therapist's hands have

37
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,218
no reason to go.

38
00:01:33,418 --> 00:01:36,655
The first second, I told myself I was wrong.

39
00:01:36,655 --> 00:01:37,464
He slipped.

40
00:01:37,464 --> 00:01:38,936
You're imagining it.

41
00:01:38,936 --> 00:01:40,707
Don't make it weird.

42
00:01:40,907 --> 00:01:44,534
The second time, there was no mistake left to believe

43
00:01:44,534 --> 00:01:45,039
in.

44
00:01:46,739 --> 00:01:48,146
And I didn't move.

45
00:01:48,346 --> 00:01:49,556
I didn't scream.

46
00:01:49,556 --> 00:01:50,765
I didn't sit up.

47
00:01:50,765 --> 00:01:53,032
I didn't say his name or stop.

48
00:01:53,032 --> 00:01:54,392
I'm a grown woman.

49
00:01:54,392 --> 00:01:57,868
I've stood up to principals, landlords, police

50
00:01:57,868 --> 00:01:59,153
officers, judges.

51
00:01:59,153 --> 00:02:02,627
I have never been afraid to open my mouth.

52
00:02:02,827 --> 00:02:06,174
But on that table, my mouth wouldn't open.

53
00:02:06,174 --> 00:02:08,804
My arms were heavy like wet sand.

54
00:02:08,804 --> 00:02:12,948
My heart was pounding so hard I could hear it in the

55
00:02:12,948 --> 00:02:15,878
pillow, and my body just… stayed.

56
00:02:16,078 --> 00:02:18,993
I counted the holes in the face cradle.

57
00:02:18,993 --> 00:02:20,787
I listened to the music.

58
00:02:20,787 --> 00:02:24,076
I watched one strip of light under the door.

59
00:02:24,076 --> 00:02:27,739
I went somewhere far away and waited for it to be

60
00:02:27,739 --> 00:02:28,413
over.

61
00:02:28,613 --> 00:02:30,603
That's when it happened.

62
00:02:30,603 --> 00:02:32,014
Not with a fight.

63
00:02:32,014 --> 00:02:33,475
With a freeze.

64
00:02:33,675 --> 00:02:37,223
When it was done, he said, "Take your time getting

65
00:02:37,223 --> 00:02:38,501
up." Like nothing.

66
00:02:38,501 --> 00:02:40,575
Like every other Tuesday.

67
00:02:40,775 --> 00:02:41,793
I got dressed.

68
00:02:41,793 --> 00:02:42,302
I paid.

69
00:02:42,302 --> 00:02:43,547
I tipped him.

70
00:02:44,447 --> 00:02:45,379
I tipped him.

71
00:02:45,379 --> 00:02:48,760
I've replayed that more than anything else.

72
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:52,807
I walked to my car, locked the doors, and sat there

73
00:02:52,807 --> 00:02:55,900
with my keys in my lap for forty minutes.

74
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:56,880
I didn't cry.

75
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,464
I didn't call anyone.

76
00:02:58,464 --> 00:02:59,594
I just sat.

77
00:02:59,794 --> 00:03:03,717
And a voice in my head asked the question I would hear

78
00:03:03,717 --> 00:03:05,605
a lot more after that day:

79
00:03:05,605 --> 00:03:07,867
Why didn't you do anything?

80
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:11,306
For weeks, I didn't do anything.

81
00:03:11,506 --> 00:03:12,678
I went to work.

82
00:03:12,678 --> 00:03:14,709
I signed permission slips.

83
00:03:14,709 --> 00:03:15,413
I cooked.

84
00:03:15,413 --> 00:03:17,835
From the outside I looked fine.

85
00:03:17,835 --> 00:03:22,054
Inside, my thoughts ran like cars on a freeway with no

86
00:03:22,054 --> 00:03:22,822
exits.

87
00:03:23,022 --> 00:03:23,939
Was it real?

88
00:03:23,939 --> 00:03:25,314
Did I lead him on?

89
00:03:25,314 --> 00:03:26,917
Who would believe me?

90
00:03:26,917 --> 00:03:28,216
He has a license.

91
00:03:28,216 --> 00:03:31,571
I have a temper, and everybody knows it.

92
00:03:31,771 --> 00:03:35,169
I'd sit on the edge of my bed for an hour and not

93
00:03:35,169 --> 00:03:36,995
remember sitting down.

94
00:03:37,195 --> 00:03:39,803
Finally, I told my boyfriend, Andre.

95
00:03:39,803 --> 00:03:43,944
I chose the words carefully, like setting down glass.

96
00:03:44,144 --> 00:03:45,105
He was quiet.

97
00:03:45,105 --> 00:03:48,067
Then he asked, not mean, just tired:

98
00:03:48,517 --> 00:03:49,710
ANDRE: What did you have on?

99
00:03:51,410 --> 00:03:52,015
A sheet.

100
00:03:52,015 --> 00:03:53,302
I had on a sheet.

101
00:03:53,302 --> 00:03:55,876
That's what you wear at a massage.

102
00:03:55,876 --> 00:03:58,295
That's what everybody wears.

103
00:03:58,495 --> 00:04:01,360
I know he didn't mean to put it on me.

104
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:04,903
But that question landed right where the freeze

105
00:04:04,903 --> 00:04:05,958
already lived.

106
00:04:05,958 --> 00:04:09,803
Because underneath what did you have on is what did

107
00:04:09,803 --> 00:04:11,535
you do to cause it.

108
00:04:11,735 --> 00:04:13,144
Then I told my dad.

109
00:04:13,144 --> 00:04:14,702
My dad loves me loud.

110
00:04:14,702 --> 00:04:17,742
He wanted to drive over there that night.

111
00:04:17,742 --> 00:04:19,822
When I said no, he said,

112
00:04:20,272 --> 00:04:22,484
DAD: Then let it go, baby girl.

113
00:04:22,484 --> 00:04:24,270
DAD: You know how you get.

114
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:27,293
DAD: Don't make it bigger than it is.

115
00:04:27,743 --> 00:04:31,383
Between the two of them, I heard the same message:

116
00:04:31,383 --> 00:04:35,396
Either you caused it, or you're overreacting to it.

117
00:04:35,596 --> 00:04:37,127
So I went quiet again.

118
00:04:37,127 --> 00:04:39,933
And the quiet got heavier every day.

119
00:04:41,133 --> 00:04:44,813
One night, I read about something called the freeze

120
00:04:44,813 --> 00:04:45,763
response.

121
00:04:45,963 --> 00:04:49,756
When the brain decides a threat can't be fought or

122
00:04:49,756 --> 00:04:52,335
outrun, it can shut the body down.

123
00:04:52,335 --> 00:04:53,624
Muscles go heavy.

124
00:04:53,624 --> 00:04:54,838
The voice locks.

125
00:04:54,838 --> 00:04:56,279
It isn't agreement.

126
00:04:56,279 --> 00:04:57,644
It isn't weakness.

127
00:04:57,644 --> 00:05:01,358
It's survival, happening faster than thought.

128
00:05:01,558 --> 00:05:05,563
I sat on my kitchen floor and cried for the first time

129
00:05:05,563 --> 00:05:06,749
since the table.

130
00:05:06,749 --> 00:05:08,603
Not because I was broken.

131
00:05:08,603 --> 00:05:11,722
Because I finally understood I wasn't.

132
00:05:11,922 --> 00:05:13,313
I didn't do nothing.

133
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:17,160
My body was protecting me the only way it knew how.

134
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:21,293
The next morning I called the state licensing board.

135
00:05:21,293 --> 00:05:22,805
I filed a complaint.

136
00:05:22,805 --> 00:05:24,545
I made a police report.

137
00:05:24,545 --> 00:05:28,553
I wrote it all down, every date, every detail I could

138
00:05:28,553 --> 00:05:29,533
remember.

139
00:05:29,733 --> 00:05:33,360
And the people around me said what they always say.

140
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:36,986
"You're doing too much." "Why now?" "You waited all

141
00:05:36,986 --> 00:05:40,343
that time, and now you want to blow it up?"

142
00:05:40,543 --> 00:05:41,633
I didn't rush.

143
00:05:41,633 --> 00:05:45,369
I carried it by myself until it got too heavy to

144
00:05:45,369 --> 00:05:45,836
carry.

145
00:05:45,836 --> 00:05:47,392
That's not too much.

146
00:05:47,392 --> 00:05:50,027
That's the exact right amount.

147
00:05:50,227 --> 00:05:51,518
Andre came around.

148
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:54,613
Weeks later he sat next to me and said,

149
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:56,909
ANDRE: I asked you the wrong question.

150
00:05:56,909 --> 00:05:57,805
ANDRE: I'm sorry.

151
00:05:58,255 --> 00:06:00,814
My dad still doesn't fully get it.

152
00:06:00,814 --> 00:06:03,147
But he drove me to the hearing.

153
00:06:03,147 --> 00:06:05,481
Love doesn't always understand.

154
00:06:05,481 --> 00:06:07,964
Sometimes love just shows up.

155
00:06:08,864 --> 00:06:13,417
The Bible says, "The Lord is nigh unto them that are

156
00:06:13,417 --> 00:06:18,146
of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite

157
00:06:18,146 --> 00:06:20,285
spirit." Psalm 34:18.

158
00:06:20,485 --> 00:06:22,614
And I hold on to this one:

159
00:06:22,614 --> 00:06:26,546
"For there is nothing covered, that shall not be

160
00:06:26,546 --> 00:06:30,886
revealed; neither hid, that shall not be known." Luke

161
00:06:30,886 --> 00:06:31,596
12:2.

162
00:06:31,796 --> 00:06:34,295
If you froze, you did not consent.

163
00:06:34,295 --> 00:06:36,795
If you waited, you were not lying.

164
00:06:36,795 --> 00:06:40,770
If you finally spoke, you were not doing too much.

165
00:06:40,970 --> 00:06:44,671
Have you ever been asked the wrong question after

166
00:06:44,671 --> 00:06:46,635
something happened to you?

167
00:06:46,635 --> 00:06:48,448
Tell me in the comments.

168
00:06:48,448 --> 00:06:52,301
Somebody reading needs to know they're not the only

169
00:06:52,301 --> 00:06:52,903
one.

170
00:06:53,603 --> 00:06:57,396
If this happened to you, you don't have to carry it

171
00:06:57,396 --> 00:06:57,842
alone.

172
00:06:57,842 --> 00:07:00,223
Open the Community Covenant app.

173
00:07:00,223 --> 00:07:02,528
The link is in the description.

174
00:07:02,528 --> 00:07:06,322
If you're in the U.S. and want to talk to a lawyer,

175
00:07:06,322 --> 00:07:10,041
the free legal referral form is in the description

176
00:07:10,041 --> 00:07:10,338
too.

177
00:07:10,338 --> 00:07:13,314
It's free to ask and free to be matched.

178
00:07:13,314 --> 00:07:17,107
We are not attorneys, and this is not legal advice.

179
00:07:17,107 --> 00:07:19,936
It's a referral to someone who is.

180
00:07:20,136 --> 00:07:24,120
If you're in danger right now, call 911.

181
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:29,398
In the U.S., you can call the National Sexual Assault

182
00:07:29,398 --> 00:07:34,378
Hotline at 1-800-656-4673, any time, day or night.

183
00:07:34,378 --> 00:07:39,358
If you're thinking about hurting yourself, call or

184
00:07:39,358 --> 00:07:40,554
text 988.
